//	Implicit multiplication and prefix absorption ( SPEC §2.2, §4.2 )

//	Adjacent numerics multiply
( 2 3 4 )
( 'r = 2 )
( 2 π r )

//	A prefix absorbs the run of bare numerics after it: this is cos( 2 × π ),
//	not cos( 2 ) × π
( cos 2 π )
( cos 0 )
( cos π )

//	A parenthesised argument ends the run, so this is cos( 0 ) × 3
( cos(0) 3 )

//	A function result also ends the run: 2 × π × cos( 0 )
( 2 π cos 0 )
